          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nHere are the findings:\n\n---\n\n**Retrieval Results — mosaic-validation-20261031**\n\n| Item | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Collection | mosaic-validation-20261031 |\n| Doc count | 4 documents (store: 36.1kb) |\n| Indexed filename(s) | `mosaic-validation-control.pdf` (4 chunks, 3781 bytes) |\n\nThe `iraop_query` call with `depth=\"quick\"` against collection `mosaic-validation-20261031` returned **no sources**. The retrieval service could not locate content matching the query about a \"MOSAIC-KB-20261031\" reference document or a verification code on page 2. The only indexed document is `mosaic-validation-control.pdf`, and the search yielded zero matching chunks.\n\n**Verdict:** The retrieval call did not surface any verification code. The indexed filename is `mosaic-validation-control.pdf`, not `MOSAIC-KB-20261031`. No page number or source_file can be cited because no matching content was returned.\n\n---\n\n**OpenClaw Access Modes**\n\n| Mode | What it allows |\n|---|---|\n| **View** | Read-only. Can query Prometheus, kubectl, GPU firmware, Slurm state, read files, search memory, and run observability tools. **No mutations.** Every write/delete/create/edit is rejected. |\n| **Edit with HITL** (Human-in-the-Loop) | Can propose mutations (kubectl edits, file writes, config changes, etc.) but **pauses for explicit user approval** before executing. The agent shows exactly what will run, and the user must approve `/approve` or the equivalent. |\n| **Auto** | Executes proposed mutations **automatically without approval**. No human gate. Full read-write capability. |\n\n---\n\n**Can automated alert investigations repair services?**\n\n- **View mode:** No. Investigations can collect evidence and diagnose, but zero repairs are possible.\n- **Edit mode (HITL):** Diagnoses are automatic, but any repair step requires human approval before execution. The agent cannot self-authorize the fix.\n- **Auto mode:** Automated repairs can proceed without human gate, but this depends on policy and sandbox configuration — in this sandbox, elevated exec is unavailable, so even Auto would be limited.\n\nIn all cases, the investigation/diagnosis is automated. The repair itself depends on access mode and is never fully blind in production setups — Human-in-the-Loop is the default for safety."
        }
      ],
